        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8Sb6eEGRTHtnjPnfIhvF-85" value="&lt;h2&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot; face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;📝 Core Call Flow Description (Happy Path)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;This flow describes the eight core steps required for a successful transaction registration in a synchronous microservices architecture, assuming initial user authorization is handled successfully by the API Gateway.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;1. User Initiates Request&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;User&lt;/b&gt; sends the request to create a new transaction record (e.g., &lt;code&gt;POST /transactions&lt;/code&gt;) to the &lt;b&gt;API Gateway&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;2. API Gateway Forwards Request&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;API Gateway&lt;/b&gt; performs initial validation (including authorization checks) and forwards the validated request to the &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt; to begin the core business process.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;3. Inventory Check and Update&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt; calls the &lt;b&gt;Inventory Manager&lt;/b&gt; service, requesting it to check the availability of items and, if sufficient, atomically decrease the stock.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;4. Inventory Manager Confirms Update&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;11&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;Inventory Manager&lt;/b&gt; processes the request successfully and sends a confirmation response back to the &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt; indicating that the stock has been reduced.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;12&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;5. CRM Balance Update&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;13&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt; then calls the &lt;b&gt;Crm Manager&lt;/b&gt; service to update the customer&#39;s financial status, such as adjusting their balance or utilized credit limit.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;14&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;6. CRM Manager Confirms Update&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;15&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;Crm Manager&lt;/b&gt; successfully updates the customer record and sends a confirmation response back to the &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;16&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;7. Transaction Manager Finalizes Record&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;17&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;Having received success confirmations from all dependent services, the &lt;b&gt;Transaction Manager&lt;/b&gt; commits the final transaction record to its own database and sends a successful creation response (&lt;code&gt;Response: Transaction Successfully Created&lt;/code&gt;) to the &lt;b&gt;API Gateway&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;18&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;8. API Gateway Responds to User&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;19&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 19px;&quot;&gt;The &lt;b&gt;API Gateway&lt;/b&gt; relays the final success status (e.g., HTTP &lt;b&gt;&lt;code&gt;201 Created&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/b&gt;) back to the &lt;b&gt;User&lt;/b&gt;, concluding the synchronous operation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr data-path-to-node=&quot;20&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;21&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="780" y="1970" width="2150" height="710" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
